<properties xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xsi:noNamespaceSchemaLocation="https://developer.garmin.com/downloads/connect-iq/resources.xsd">
    <!-- Overrides for the watches that have no hands of their own.

         Only what actually differs is here; every other property comes from
         resources/properties.xml, so the stored values stay indices into the
         same enums and a ring set on one watch means the same on another. -->

    <!-- 0 off, 1 white, 2 dark. Kept in sync with StatMap.Backing.

         **On by default here, where it is off on the Crossover.** There the
         setting decides whether to light the dots behind two brass hands, and
         off is the plainer face. Here it decides whether the face shows the
         time at all.

         **And dark rather than white, which is the opposite of the obvious.**
         A drawn hand has to be found among ~1400 lit crosses, and a bright
         hand is more of what is already there - measured against the mockups
         at six times of day, the white pair reads as a faint streak and is
         genuinely hard to pick out. Cut out of the field instead, the hands
         are the only dark shape on a lit disc and they read at a glance. It
         holds in all three power modes and costs less light in every one:
         4.12% against 4.50% awake, 3.94% against 4.33% always-on.

         White is still there for anyone who wants the Crossover's own pair. -->
    <property id="handBacking" type="number">2</property>
</properties>
